# rlgrieve.msg - Inspector Marta Grieve, Licensing Office of the NCR Council
# Plain ASCII only: the English Fallout 2 fonts have no umlauts or typographic quotes.

{100}{}{(A woman in a pressed NCR jacket sits at a folding table with a stack of forms and a rubber stamp.) Inspector Grieve, Licensing Office. Establishment Number Nine is vacant. The Republic does not forbid what it can regulate. You want to apply?}
{101}{}{I want the license for Number Nine.}
{102}{}{[Speech] Mr. Westin will vouch for me. Ask him.}
{103}{}{I'll open without your paper.}
{104}{}{Your application is on my desk. The Republic is thorough. }
{105}{}{Good day, Inspector.}
{106}{}{Stamp?}
{107}{}{ week(s), and then you'll have your number.}

# The proper way
{110}{}{The fee is $}
{111}{}{File the application. Here's $}
{112}{}{[Barter] File it, and here's $300 for you to find it on top of the pile.}
{113}{}{Let's talk about something else.}
{114}{}{(She stamps three forms and puts them in three different folders.) Three weeks. And remember the condition: an infirmary. Weekly examinations are the law. Without them the license is paper.}
{115}{}{(The money disappears into a folder marked "Administrative Costs".) One week. The Republic can be quick when it's motivated. The infirmary is still the law.}
{117}{}{, three weeks' processing, and one condition: an infirmary with weekly examinations of everyone who works there. The Republic wants order, not people. Its words, not mine.}
{118}{}{.}

# Westin
{120}{}{(Two days later a rider from the Westin ranch brings a letter. Grieve reads it twice and stamps your license without a word.) Mr. Westin expects the use of the private rooms and five percent. He says you'll know what that means.}

# Without a license
{130}{}{Then Number Nine is an unlicensed house in the Bazaar, next to Vortis' pens. The police will come more often. The League for a Pure Republic will come immediately. I'm telling you as a courtesy.}
{131}{}{Let them come.}
{132}{}{(Grieve closes her folder, stands up and leaves without another word. The number over the door stays painted over.)}

# Opening
{190}{}{There's a woman at the door with a cook's forearms and a list of every caravan master between Redding and the Hub. Dora Quist. She's been waiting for Number Nine to open.}
{191}{}{Let her in.}

# Look
{300}{}{A woman in a pressed NCR jacket behind a folding table full of forms.}
{301}{}{Inspector Marta Grieve of the Council's Licensing Office. She can make a house legal with one stamp.}
